message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Aging-like BAC sectors and load×gain Gompertz regimes on one shared subsystem toy"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  On one shared subsystem toy, do aging-like Bounded Adaptive Coherence
  sectors coincide with load×gain regimes that produce Gompertz-like hazard,
  or do the two objects carve different regions? They carve different regions.
  The five-index weight matrix of Thesis #18 is read by that deposit's
  grounded-Laplacian classifier and, on the same paths, by the load×gain
  residual test of Thesis #13. At zero damage-rate gain the exponential map is
  an exact Gompertz hazard on every class, and only global decay is
  aging-like. At gain 0.01 the aging-like path fails the chi-squared budget
  while an uneven path classed neither still passes. On a 13 by 13 rate grid
  at gain 0.02 the two sets are disjoint. No rejuvenation claim. Not a
  medical device. No document DOI.
keywords:
